    ],
    "notes": "Named as the active substance of the formulations. The section gives the total active substance content as 1 to 98 wt. %, in particular 10 to 95 wt. %, of the plant protection agent; that is a formulation range in weight percent, which the quantity schema cannot carry, so quantity is null. [0102] of this section names only what an additive does and no material at all: surface-active substances, wetting agents, emulsifiers and dispersant, viscosity-modifying additives, thickeners and rheology modifiers, antifoaming agents, antifreeze agents, pH adjusting agents, stabilizers, anticaking agents and biocides or preservatives. All twelve are treated alike and none has a record, so no compound is recorded from that paragraph."
  },
