    "tags": [
      "compound_class:other"
    ],
    "notes": "Named in the plural as a fertilizer used as a solid carrier, so it denotes urea and urea type fertilizers rather than urea specifically, and is left unresolved. Recorded as printed. The policy applied throughout these sections: a chemical or material class named as an ingredient with no member of it named is recorded once and left unresolved; a class whose members the sentence goes on to name is not recorded and only its members are; a word that names only a function is never recorded. ureas is a class of the first kind here and has a record on that basis. The same word is printed again at line 708, outside this section, in [0162], where it denotes the substituted urea class of herbicides offered as mixing partners. The same policy gives that occurrence a record too, but it names a different substance from the urea fertilizer meant here, so the two must not be spelled the same, or they merge into one record for two different things."
  },
